    {
      "kind": "explain",
      "text": {
        "es": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "La "
          },
          {
            "kind": "term",
            "id": "interference",
            "text": "interferencia"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " es poner una pieza tuya en medio de la línea por la que el rival defiende. Aquí la torre negra de "
          },
          {
            "kind": "square",
            "square": "d8"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " defiende a su dama de "
          },
          {
            "kind": "square",
            "square": "d2"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " por la columna, y tu dama de "
          },
          {
            "kind": "square",
            "square": "e2"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " ataca a esa dama. El caballo salta a "
          },
          {
            "kind": "square",
            "square": "d6"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " con jaque y corta la columna. Si el peón o el alfil lo capturan, la columna sigue cortada y pierden la dama. Lo mejor es capturar con la torre, pero tras el cambio de damas las negras han dado una torre por un caballo y un peón."
          }
        ],
        "en": [
          {
            "kind": "term",
            "id": "interference",
            "text": "Interference"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " means putting one of your pieces in the middle of the line your opponent defends along. Here the black rook on "
          },
          {
            "kind": "square",
            "square": "d8"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " defends its queen on "
          },
          {
            "kind": "square",
            "square": "d2"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " along the file, and your queen on "
          },
          {
            "kind": "square",
            "square": "e2"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " attacks that queen. The knight jumps to "
          },
          {
            "kind": "square",
            "square": "d6"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "text": " with check and cuts the file. If the pawn or the bishop takes it, the file stays cut and the queen is lost. Taking with the rook is best, but after the queens come off Black has given a rook for a knight and a pawn."
          }
        ]
      },
